:"Supply-chain basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product research"},{"text":"Market analysis"},{"text":"Vendor coordination"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Basic sales/product knowledge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"Power BI fundamentals"},{"text":"SQL basics"},{"text":"ERP awareness"},{"text":"Digital product management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Internship in an Ayurveda/herbal organization"},{"text":"Exposure to quality or manufacturing"},{"text":"One herbal-product market-analysis project"},{"text":"One inventory/quality dashboard"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Herbal Products Executive","Product/Quality Specialist","Regulatory or Product Management","Herbal & Wellness Industry Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"For the 2026–2046 market, the strongest profile is not simply “Ayurveda product sales.” It is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Herbal Science","Quality","Regulatory Knowledge","Product Management","Digital Analytics."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"That combination can create opportunities across Ayurvedic medicines, herbal wellness, natural personal care, nutraceutical-adjacent businesses, research, quality, regulatory affairs and herbal-product management, while keeping regulated formulation and therapeutic responsibilities with appropriately qualified professionals."}]}]}